[N 29-30 Excavation Site: Wetlands]
[D Forever Alliance 1-30 (Braedyn)\\Menethil pickups, the walk to Whelgar's dig site and a full run of the Excavation Site (Forever's new Wetlands five-man: Saltspine, Shadetooth, the Highland Horror and the Relic Guardian), then the hand-ins, the shaman's Call of Water errands and the boat to Southshore.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel 29-30|r  -  you step off the Auberdine boat at Menethil Harbor with chapters 20 and 21 behind you; hearth = Sentinel Hill and it STAYS there (the shaman hearths to it from Loch Modan for the Forgotten Shrine near the end of this chapter). This is the dungeon chapter for the Excavation Site, a NEW Forever five-man in the hills above Whelgar's dig site: about 17,700 quest XP handed in here at quest level (18,300 with the relic quest, 21,500 with the optional group quest Gleaning Our Future; the level-20 and level-24 quests pay less at your level), shaman +6,200 from Call of Water at quest level (the whole finale and the Water Totem are in this chapter), and 7,500 XP of quests picked up for chapters 24 and 25.
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r the DB has no creature rows, spawns or drop tables for this dungeon and there are no coordinates inside. Boss order and abilities come from Icy Veins, Method, kami-labs and a Wowhead-based article; drop rates from the item tooltips and kami-labs. All of it is |cffffcc00per those pages, unverified in game|r; where they disagree the line says so.
[OC]|cffffcc00Carried in:|r Songblade Search (95772), Highland Hides (98815), Horrors in the Highland (95646), Gleaning Our Future (98310) if you took it, shaman Call of Water (94500, the filled Blue Waterskin).
[OC]|cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r the run needs five: your tank friend, the two of you and two more (finder level 26; Method and the article also mention a meeting stone at the foot of the climb). The quests need 24, but the last boss is level 31 and Wowhead advises against entering at 24: you are well past that. Bring food, water, a repair and a full ammo count.

[OC]|cffffffffMenethil Harbor|r  -  three pickups and a shopping stop, all within 8 units of the dock
At [TAR1480 Caitlin Grassman], [QT95737] [QA95647 Lost in the Thicket Things] (2,500 XP: her husband Ardin stands on a platform beside the last boss inside the Excavation Site; he is the hand-in and gives you Heartwoven for her) [G11.9,58.8 Wetlands]
At [TAR1217 Glorin Steelbrow], [QA322 Blessed Arm] (1,200 XP: the Crate of Lightforge Ingots goes to Grimand Elmore in Stormwind, chapter 25) [G10.6,60.6 Wetlands]
At [TAR2911 Archaeologist Flagongut], [QT942] [QA943 The Absent Minded Prospector] (2,400 XP: the Stone of Relu and Flagongut's Fossil, both on your way to the dungeon; hand in here after the run. 942 was a level-20 quest and pays little now) [G10.8,60.4 Wetlands]
[OC]|cffffcc00Label (943):|r the fossil is one click beside Whelgar (|cff66ff66normal|r); the stone drops from the four raptor types of the valley and dig site and |cffffcc00the DB gives no rate|r - kill the ones you pass and take what comes; no stone after the run, skip the hand-in. The rewards (Relic Blade, Skullchipper, Archaeologist's Gown) are item-level 20: vendor all three
[O]|cffffcc00Food for the run:|r cook a stack of Mithril Head Trout (+20 attack power) if Cooking is 175, otherwise Succulent Pork Ribs / Longjaw; while the group forms, fish off the dock for more trout ([TAR3178 Stuart Fleming] at 8.0,58.4: Nightcrawlers) [G8.0,58.4 Wetlands]
[A Hunter] At [TAR1462 Edwina Monzor] the fletcher, buy 600+ of your level-25 ammo for the run (the gunsmith [TAR1461 Murndan Derth] sells bullets) [G11.1,58.3 Wetlands]
[OC]Food and water from the general vendor [TAR1452 Gruham Rumdnul] (12.1,58.0), repairs at [TAR1450 Brahnmar] (11.5,59.9), then empty your bags

[OC]|cffffffffThe dig site|r  -  the road east and down into the valley, the same 3-minute walk as chapter 18. Raptors are level 22-29 and safe; the Goaz Warders (level 32 elites) look like statues that only wake with a Goaz Stone (chapter 18)
Follow the road east to the turn-off above the dig site [G34.1,40.8 Wetlands]
Kill [TAR1022 Mottled Scytheclaw] and [TAR1023 Mottled Razormaw] on the way down for the Stone of Relu (the Mottled Raptors and Screechers west of here drop it too) [G34.1,48.2 Wetlands]
Cook to 175: at your campfire by Whelgar's tents, cook Curiously Tasty Omelets until Cooking 175 - the Mottled raptors you kill on this walk and the Stone of Relu kills all drop Raptor Eggs (rate not in the DB: take what falls, no farming). At 175 the Recipe: Mithril Head Trout from chapter 9 opens (+20 attack power, you are 29-30) [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]
At [TAR1077 Prospector Whelgar], [QA98313 For Further Study] (the Whelgar Relic Package goes to Historian Karnik in Ironforge, chapter 24; its XP is not in the DB) [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]
Click Flagongut's Fossil lying beside Whelgar [QC943] [G38.9,52.2 Wetlands]
[OC]Prehistoric Prism (98824) is the follow-up to Lost Relic Carry (kami-labs and the article call it step 2 of 2, unverified), so Whelgar offers it after the run, below. If he already offers it now, take it and skip the later accept
Follow the track east and up to the dungeon door; Icy Veins puts it just south of the Thelgen Rock cavern and the DB at 47.8,56.2 [G47.8,56.2 Wetlands]

[OC]|cffffffffExcavation Site: Wetlands|r  -  |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r, finder level 26, ~20-35 minutes (Method), one outdoor map of four zones (Lost Marsh, Stalker's Thicket, Site of the Guardian, Lost Dig Site). Four bosses in a line: Saltspine, Shadetooth, the Highland Horror (a quest boss that drops no gear) and the Relic Guardian. Levels: Highland Horror 28 (the DB), Relic Guardian 31 (Method, Wowhead); no source gives the others. Nothing is picked up at the door
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Lost in the Thicket Things (95647) then Heartwoven (95809) - |cff66ff66normal|r: Ardin Grassman, on a platform beside the Relic Guardian, takes the first and hands you the Reed-woven Heart for the second
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Songblade Search (95772) then Fallen in the Fen (95795) - |cff66ff66normal|r: Daewyn Songblade lies in a camping hut just past Shadetooth (Icy Veins); the second goes to Dorin in Lakeshire, chapter 25
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Horrors in the Highland (95646) - |cff66ff66normal|r in one pass: the Highland Horror drops the Horrible Rootcore 64% of the time and it is a quest item, so each of you rolls your own; he stands at a camp hut after Shadetooth (Icy Veins)
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Highland Hides (98815) - |cffffcc00grind risk|r: 4 Thicket Raptor Hides from Shadetooth and the Thicket Lurkers, Hunters and Matriarchs; the DB has no rates (kami-labs shows 5.5% on Shadetooth himself). Kill every Thicket pack you pass; with fewer than 4 at the end, abandon it [QS98815] - it is the smallest quest here (1,150 XP)
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Lost Relic Carry (95810, 630 XP) then Prehistoric Prism (98824, 3,150 XP) - |cffffcc00luck, 26.78%|r: the Titan Relic drops from the last boss only and the tooltip does not mark it a Quest Item, so expect a roll, and each of you needs one. Right-click it for 95810, hand it in at Whelgar and he offers the Prism, a carry to High Explorer Magellas in Ironforge (chapter 24). A miss costs a second clear: worth it for the shaman (the Prism's Heavehammer is a 27.7 dps 2H mace with +32 attack power), for the hunter it is only the XP

[OC]|cffffffffThe run|r  -  Saltspine first, on the crocolisk lake of the Lost Marsh. Young Riptooths come in threes with Fatal Bite (kill one at a time, no full AoE), Marsh Skulkers cast Muculent Rot (less Spirit and Stamina) and Skulkers and Elder Crocolisks use Tendon Rip, a 71% slow (Method)
[OC]|cffffcc00Saltspine|r patrols the lake edge: Dust Storm (-25% hit chance for anyone in melee range per Icy Veins; Method reads it as a threat cut - either way casters and the hunter stay out of melee), Tendon Rip and Fatal Bite on the tank. Easy once the lake trash is dead; never pull him with a second pack
[OC]|cffffcc00Stalker's Thicket|r: Thicket Lurkers and Stalkers come in threes and hide invisibly in the tall grass until you step close - walk the path, not the grass. Thicket Hunters put Infected Wound (a disease) on the tank: cleanse it. Matriarchs and Lurkers apply Rend Flesh, a strong bleed
[OC]|cffffcc00Shadetooth|r (the hardest fight here per Icy Veins; patrols the raptor path with two Thicket Hunters): clear the raptors stealthed in the bushes and the crocodile den first, then kill the two Hunters before him (they can be crowd-controlled). His Terrifying Roar is an undispellable 5-second fear that runs you into the grass packs: the shaman drops a |cff66ff66Tremor Totem|r (Method). Rend hurts the tank; he enrages at 20% (Method) or 30% (Icy Veins) - stuns and slows. The article: pull him to the cove on the left after clearing it, the Hunters cannot swim
[OC]|cffffcc00After Shadetooth|r: Daewyn's hut comes right after him (Icy Veins) and the Highland Horror is the third boss, before the Relic Guardian (kami-labs, the article). Dragonmaw Saboteurs throw ground bombs (step out of the channel), Warders Mortal Strike and Net you (Blessing of Freedom breaks the net), Thaumaturgists come with a fire elemental: kill it first (Method; the sources do not say where they stand)
[OC]|cffffcc00Highland Horror|r (level 28 per the DB; Entangling Roots and Wild Regeneration per Method): the slimes around him are separate pulls, do not wake them early. Kill him fast and loot the Horrible Rootcore. The DB also pins a Highland Horror at 49.5,59.7 in the open Wetlands, just outside the door: if you ever see one out there, kill it there
[OC]|cffffcc00Relic Guardian|r (level 31, a construct that starts inactive): use the panel on his right (the Archival or Titan Control Panel) to start him. Thunderclap slows and cuts attack speed within ~10 yards, Arcing Smash cleaves the front (face him away from the group), Knock Away drops the tank's threat, War Stomp and a tank stun come now and then. He can be stunned, slowed and crowd-controlled; Concussive Shot or Earthbind Totem can kite him (Method, Icy Veins)

Kill the Thicket packs and Shadetooth for four Thicket Raptor Hides [QC98815]
At Daewyn Songblade's hut, [QT95772] [QA95795 Fallen in the Fen]
Kill the Highland Horror and loot the Horrible Rootcore [QC95646]
At [TAR262681 Ardin Grassman] on the platform beside the Relic Guardian, [QT95647] [QA95809 Heartwoven] (no spawn in the DB)
[OC]Loot the Titan Relic from the Relic Guardian (26.78%) and right-click it: that starts Lost Relic Carry (95810), handed in at Whelgar below
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot calls (rolls):|r |cff66ff66Supple Bellyskin Leggings|r (Saltspine, leather legs 92 armor +6 Str +14 Sta; Strength is two attack power for a shaman): better than Duty Bound Leggings. |cff66ff66Garb of Florid Feathers|r (Shadetooth, leather chest 105 armor +9 Agi +15 Int) only if you do not wear Raptorbane Armor (+16 attack power): the two are close. Ring of Power Regulation (+6 spell damage, 3 mana per 5 sec) only for an empty ring slot; Glinteye Slippers (cloth) only for bare boots. Saltscale Girdle, Raptorclaw Greaves and Reliquary Mantle are MAIL, Raptor's Gaze is an off-hand a two-hander cannot use, the gun is a hunter's: pass
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Loot calls (rolls):|r |cff66ff66Golemsight Long Gun|r (Relic Guardian, 16.6 dps +6 Agi, requires 28): roll Need if you use guns, it beats Raptor's End (bow 12.1 dps). Supple Bellyskin Leggings (Saltspine, +6 Str +14 Sta) only over legs with no Stamina: Duty Bound's Agility is better for damage. Garb of Florid Feathers (Shadetooth, leather chest +9 Agi +15 Int) only if you do not wear Raptorbane Armor (+16 attack power). Saltscale Girdle, Raptorclaw Greaves and Reliquary Mantle are MAIL, Raptor's Gaze is an off-hand, Ring of Power Regulation and Glinteye Slippers are caster items: pass

[OC]|cffffffffAfter the run|r  -  the door is 20 units north of the Dun Algaz pass and 18 units south-west of Rethiel's clearing; everything below is one walk north-west to Menethil. The shaman goes south first for Call of Water (the cave is 27 units from the door), the hunter straight to Rethiel
[A Shaman] Walk south-east across the valley toward the falls and Hervdana's cave; stay west of Golm's box (x64-69, y63-73) until you are level with the cave [G60.4,70.9 Wetlands]
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r Gleaning Our Future: use the Goaz Stone beside [TAR271462 Golm], kill what wakes and loot the heart (level 32 ELITE, no HP in the DB; needs the other three hearts from chapter 19) - the whole group walks this detour together [QC98310,3] [G67.2,70.0 Wetlands]
[A Shaman] At [TAR258203 Hervdana Saegrund], [QT94500] [QA94501 Call of Water] (the Vial of Purest Water goes to Norric Lochthane at the north end of Loch Modan, below) [G65.8,76.4 Wetlands]
[A Shaman] Walk north-west up the valley to Rethiel's clearing at the road junction (about 37 units, 4 minutes) [G56.4,40.4 Wetlands]
[A Hunter] Walk north-east up the valley to Rethiel's clearing at the road junction [G56.4,40.4 Wetlands]
At [TAR1244 Rethiel the Greenwarden], [QT95646] [G56.4,40.4 Wetlands]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear (95646):|r take |cff66ff66Ironwood Destroyer|r (2H mace 22.2 dps, +19 Nature damage): a small step up from Glacial Stone (21.0 dps with a frost proc) until the Prism's Heavehammer. Curl of Life (ring +5 Sta +5 spell damage) only for an empty ring slot; Hornbeam Heft is a spell-damage one-hander: pass
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Gear (95646):|r hunters cannot use maces, so Ironwood Destroyer is vendor fodder; Curl of Life (ring +5 Sta +5 spell damage) only for an empty ring slot; Hornbeam Heft (1H axe 11.5 dps, +26 spell damage) loses to what you carry: vendor
[O]At [TAR1077 Prospector Whelgar], [QA95810 Lost Relic Carry] [QT95810] [QA98824 Prehistoric Prism] (only with the Titan Relic; the Prism's reward is picked at Magellas in chapter 24) [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]
[O]At [TAR1077 Prospector Whelgar], [QT98310] - |cffffcc00Gear:|r Golem War Cloak (+6 Str, 72 armor) for both of you unless your cloak is better; Rune-Etched Ring (+10 Sta) only for an empty ring slot, Giantstone Medallion (neck +10 Spirit) only for a bare neck [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]
[OC]|cffffffffMenethil hand-ins|r  -  walk back west along the road (about 3 minutes)
At [TAR2094 James Halloran], [QT98815] (1,150 XP, no item reward) [G8.6,55.7 Wetlands]
At [TAR1480 Caitlin Grassman], [QT95809] - |cffffcc00Gear:|r take the Greater Healing Potion (the Mana Potion is the other choice); the fixed Satchel of Potions is a trinket that gives a random potion on a 10-minute cooldown: wear it only if your trinket slot is empty [G11.9,58.8 Wetlands]
At [TAR2911 Archaeologist Flagongut], [QT943] [G10.8,60.4 Wetlands]

[OC][A Shaman] |cffffffffShaman: Norric, the Forgotten Shrine and the Water Totem|r  -  Call of Water finishes in Loch Modan and Westfall (94501 460 XP, 94502 1,400 XP, 94503 + 94505 2,935 XP at quest level, plus the 1,400 you took at Hervdana). Flights and a hearth, no walking in the Wetlands
[A Shaman] At [TAR1571 Shellei Brondir], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Ironforge]|r [G9.5,59.7 Wetlands]
[O][A Shaman] At [TAR258098 Eldrun Stormbreaker] in the Forlorn Cavern, [T] train your level 30 spells if you are 30 [G46.6,13.4 Ironforge]
[A Shaman] At [TAR1573 Gryth Thurden], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Thelsamar]|r [G55.5,47.7 Ironforge]
